<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulugh Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1405–1445</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulugh Muhammad was a Chinggisid khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> who, after losing power in the struggles of the early 15th century, moved to the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and around 1438 founded the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a>. He defeated and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow">Vasily II of Moscow</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> in 1445, the year he was killed by his son Mahmud. Another son, Qasim, entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>'s service and received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kasimov">Kasimov</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulugh-muhammad.jpg" alt="Ulugh Muhammad" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vyacheslav Kirillin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahmud_reconstruction_(2023-03-07)_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
